 "post": {
  "title": "Is ANC worth it on budget earbuds?",
  "caption": "Is ANC worth it on budget earbuds? 🎧\n\nHow it works: a tiny mic on each earbud hears the sound around you, and the earbud plays the opposite wave, so the two cancel out.\nWhere it shines: steady, low hum (bus, metro, flights). Voices and sudden sounds still get through more.\nWhat it costs: battery. OnePlus Nord Buds 3 (₹2,799 with up to 32 dB ANC on OnePlus India) play up to 12 hours with ANC off and 8 hours with it on (earbuds alone, 50% volume, OnePlus's own tests).\n\nWorth it on a noisy commute, skip it for a quiet room. Would you pay for ANC? yes or no in the comments, and send this to the friend shopping for earbuds.",
  "keywords": [
   "is ANC worth it",
   "ANC earbuds under 3000",
   "how does ANC work",
